{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1245977-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight","id":1245977,"title":"Hedge Ghosts and Twilight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-14T11:17:19-07:00","id":1245977,"title":"Hedge Ghosts and Twilight","content":"I'm asking this here because Mage presents the most cohesive overview of various Twilight states of all the gamelines, and enough information is presented in Changeling to make sense for a Changeling game, so this question would probably never come up there. I want to reiterate that everything that follows is an attempt to reason through something for a Mage game; not an attempt at enforcing Mage rules on another gameline. <br /> <br /> Here's the question: Should Hedge Ghosts in the material be considered to be in (Fate!)Twilight?<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E states that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hedge has no Twilight state. Hedge ghosts that dematerialize are just incorporeal and invisible. A Hedge ghost that ventures into the mortal world doesn\u2019t fall into a Twilight state there, either, but it dematerializes automatically even if it doesn\u2019t know that Numen, and must spend three Glamour points to materialize for one scene; it can only do so if at least one of its spheres of Influence is present. Other ephemeral entities who end up in the Hedge automatically materialize even if they normally couldn\u2019t. </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly concerned with Hedge Ghosts in the material. Otherworlds lacking Twilight is nothing new (Hello Underworld, Shadow, etc).<br /> <br /> The Numen in question:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For 3 Glamour, the Hedge ghost fades from sight and becomes incorporeal. It may still use its Influences and any Numina that don\u2019t require touching the target or being perceived, but it can\u2019t physically interact with anything \u2014 even other incorporeal creatures. </div> </div> </div>The Numen basically reads as if it were describing entering a Twilight State, just without all of the extra rules attachments for using Manifestations, etc, which makes sense for a game of Changeling that doesn't have Twilight as a focus. I understand shaving those rules for wordcount, and handwaving it all away by saying that they aren't in Twilight resolves a lot of potential issues that come up when you have something occupying a unique Twilight state without having to explain the different phases, etc.<br /> <br /> What I'd expect from an entity in Fate!Twilight vs the realities presented in Changeling:<ul><li>Incorporeal and invisible to the material - Check</li> <li>Incorporeal and invisible to other ephemeral entities in other phases of Twilight - Check</li> <li>Can Manifest when near Resonance/Anchor/Etc - Check</li> <li>Can still use Influences and Numina that don't require interaction with the physical world - Check</li> </ul>Is it reasonable to rule that, for the purposes of a Mage game, Hedge Ghosts in the material are, in fact, in a Twilight State (just one that doesn't align with the Death/Spirit/Mind versions)?<br /> <br /> Or should I ignore all of the similarities and just write it off as other-gameline weirdness and leave them in this Twilight-but-not-really state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:41:49-07:00","id":1245996,"title":"","content":"Well it leads to a sort of weird implication that if there\u2019s a kind of entity that can exist on a Fate band of Twilight then it should be possible to translate yourself to that band with Fate, as well as all the other Twilight shenanigans. If you\u2019re comfortable with that though then it seems absolutely reasonable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:54:23-07:00","id":1246002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1245977-hedge-ghosts-and-twilight#post1245977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or should I ignore all of the similarities and just write it off as other-gameline weirdness and leave them in this Twilight-but-not-really state?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the existence of Ghostwall, the limitations of Hedge ghosts outside the Hedge, and the specific descriptive qualities of Twilight, I'd say leave it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T15:45:15-07:00","id":1246085,"title":"","content":"I'd say its a state unlike any a mage is familiar with. With scrutiny, a mage might realize the invisible ghost was less in a state and following some sort of narrative need to be intangible, whereas a Force mage might just find a peculiar force, and a Mind mage might recognize a Mind about but be super confused as to why the goetia is seemingly invisible in twilight even to them.<br /> <br /> Until someone realizes its not *in* any twilight.<br /> <br /> Hedge ghosts being new territory and breaking mage expectations makes them an instant mystery for mages, perhaps one so exciting as to trap them! A hobgoblin in need of captured mage souls in Tuscon using hedge ghosts as bait for those studying the bell? Sounds like a great curve ball.<br /> Hedge ghosts making less and less sense to a mage the more they study it is such an exciting vehicle for hubris that I'd suggest not using a fate-twilight. So niche and folksy, the misdirection they afford could be super fun! One mage may think they found sentient dark matter and another may think its simply a kind of resonance! until its too late","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}